<title>HONG KONG: Shougang Grand H1 net returns to profit.</title>
<headline>Shougang Grand H1 net returns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   5.88 gain    vs 9.54 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  15.79 gain   vs 76.51 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    39.35 profit vs 63.21 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     40.70	  vs 48.28</p>
<p>    Company name		 Shougang Concord Grand (Group) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Shougang Concord Grand is involved in property development, finance and strategic investments.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$23.46 million on translation of convertible notes and loss of HK$7.66 million on provision for premium on early redemption of convertible nots.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
